        "reference": "Job 7:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "So am I made to possess months of vanity, and wearisome nights are appointed to me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "When I lie down, I say, When shall I arise, and the night be gone? and I am full of tossings to and fro unto the dawning of the day.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust; my skin is broken, and become loathsome.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
