        "reference": "Job 7:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "When I say, My bed shall comfort me, my couch shall ease my complaint;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Then thou scarest me with dreams, and terrifiest me through visions:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "So that my soul chooseth strangling, and death rather than my life.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 7:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
